#. y1:english="\nWelcome.||Are you ready to order,{PA:10} sir?\n\n\nSir,{PA:10} you seem pretty drunk.{PA:20}||Maybe you should take it easy.\nHow about another drink,{PA:10} sir?\n...I see.{PA:20}||Come again anytime.\n\n\nYamazaki 25 Years...\nOne of Japan's best whiskys.\nThis 25-year-old whisky is||a limited edition and{PA:10}\nwas made to celebrate Suntory's||centennial anniversary.\nSo it's very difficult to come by.\nThe taste is worth the price.{PA:10}\nAccented with the subtle flavour||of the sherry barrel...\nIt has a bitter sweet taste||that lingers on your tongue.\nOne sip is enough to lift your spirits.\n\n\n\n\nYamazaki 12 Years...\nThis is a very fine whisky.\nThis whisky made its debut||in 1984 as the first Japanese\npure malt whisky.||It was made to commemorate\nthe 60th anniversary of||the Yamazaki distillery,\nwhere the first Japanese whisky||was created.\nYou can say that this represents Yamazaki.\nAs for the taste,{PA:10}||it has a mellow yet\npowerful flavour characteristic of Yamazaki.\nIt has earned quite a reputation||overseas as well as domestically.\n\n\n\n\nThe Macallan 25 Years...{PA:10}\nWould you like to hear about||the Macallan 25 Years?\nI'll tell you up front,||this stuff isn't cheap,\nbut it's worth every yen.||As you may know,\nSome of the world's foremost scotch critics||have given this scotch perfect ratings.\nThe name comes from the Gaelic,||\"Columba\" of \"Saint Columba's Hill\".\nThe name eventually changed into \"Macallan\".\n\n\n\n\nThe Macallan 12 Years...\nThis is the standard .||grade for the Macallan.\nThe alcohol content was changed from||43% Alc./Vol. to 40% Alc./Vol. last year.\nEven though it's the standard||grade for the Macallan,\nit is still of very high quality.\nThis luxurious Scotch has a wonderful taste.||It has a sweet honey-like flavour\nand a comfortable aftertaste.\nThis is the kind of single malt Scotch||that sets the standard.\n\n\n\n\nHibiki 30 Years Old...\nThis whisky received 1st place||in the World Spirit Competition.\nThis Japanese whisky has won||acclaim the world over.\nBlended mainly with Yamazaki||white oak barrel 32 years old.\nIt has a thick taste and is rich in flavor.\nSince only 2000 bottles are||manufactured every year,\nit's hard to come by.\n\n\n\n\nBallantine's 30 years old...\nIt's the world's finest blended scotch.\n32 kinds of raw malts and 5 kinds of||raw grains are used...\nand all of them are matured||for more than 30 years.\nIt's soft on the tongue,||but the flavour lingers...\nIf you like scotch,||this is a must drink.\n\n\n\n\nBallantine's 17 Years Old...\nIt's a top-notch blended scotch with 40||kinds of single malts incorporated in it.\nIt is referred to as \"The Scotch\",{PA:10}||and is favored worldwide.\nIt's a notable scotch that can truly be||called the ultimate blend.\n\n\n\n\nJack Daniel's...\nYour standard American whisky.{PA:20}||Same recipe as the old days.\nJack Daniel's is actually a type of||Tennessee whisky.\nSo it's in a different class than bourbon.\n\n\n\n\nEarly Times...\nA world renown bourbon.\nIt has the unique American edge||and a gorgeous flavour.\nIt's very reasonably priced||and quite enjoyable.\n\n\n\n\nSuntory Brandy Imperial...\nMade from carefully selected grapes and||distilled into cognac.\nThis high quality brandy is||good on-the-rocks,\nbut I recommend to drink it straight.\nEnjoy the robust aged grape flavor||and the luscious aroma.\n\n\n\n\nCourvoisier XO...\nThis cognac brandy is called \"Napoleon\",\nbecause it was much beloved||by Napoleon himself.\nXO is one of the most||expensive Courvoisiers.\nIt is very rich in flavour but has a soft,{PA:10}||pleasant taste.\nI highly recommend it.\n\n\n\n\nThe Premium Malt's...\nLuxury beer made from||high quality materials.\nThis is made with European aroma hops\nand with 1.2 times the amount of malts||used in regular beer.\nThis beer has a subtle charm to it.{PA:20}||I highly recommend it.\n\n\n\n\nCarlsberg...\nOriginally created in Denmark,{PA:10}\nit is savoured in over||140 countries worldwide.\nIt has a fresh flavour,||which is characteristic of draft beers.\nIt's a very easy-to-drink beer.\n\n\n\n\nBeefeater...\nOne of the world's most popular||brands of gin.{PA:20}\nIt goes great in a martini.\nMost bars in this town use Beefeater.\nThey say that the distilling method||is a well-kept secret.\n\n\n\n\nSKYY VODKA...\nOne of the most famous vodkas.\nIt is distilled four times||under a controlled temperature,{PA:10}\nand filtered three times.\nThis is a very smooth vodka.\nAlso, the bottle design is very fashionable.\n\n"
#: MEDIA/STGTALK/SPA/DAY_KAB0083.BIN:20_4_97
msgctxt "MEDIA/STGTALK/SPA/DAY_KAB0083.BIN::line:20_4_97"
msgid "Un bourbon de reconocida fama mundial."
msgstr ""

